+# ADR 0120: PBR Material Texture Inputs and Generated Tangent Basis
+
+Status: Accepted
+Date: 2026-08-16
+
+## Context
+
+ADR 0118 established the renderer's scene-linear color and texture-sampling
+contract. ADR 0119 then made imported tangent handedness an explicit GPU input
+and unified static and skinned material shading behind one fragment stage.
+StandardLit still exposes only scalar roughness/metallic values, however, and
+the glTF importer drops metallic-roughness textures, occlusion textures, normal
+scale, and occlusion strength. Assets without source tangents also fall back to
+screen-space derivatives instead of receiving a stable authored-style tangent
+basis.
+
+The next renderer foundation must remain format-independent: glTF, FBX, PMX,
+and engine-authored materials normalize into the same material and mesh
+contracts, and no source-format branch may enter the renderer.
+
+## Decision
+
+1. `MaterialAsset` advances from schema v2 to schema v3. Per ADR 0115, readers
+   accept exactly the current version; v2 is rejected rather than kept behind a
+   compatibility reader. Stable material Asset IDs do not change.
+2. StandardLit adds two optional linear-data texture slots:
+   `metallic_roughness_texture` and `occlusion_texture`. The packed
+   metallic/roughness contract uses green for roughness and blue for metallic;
+   occlusion uses red. Missing slots resolve to white so existing scalar factors
+   preserve their previous result.
+3. Material schema v3 also stores `normal_scale` and `occlusion_strength`.
+   Normal scale multiplies tangent-space X/Y before normalization. Occlusion
+   strength is clamped to `[0, 1]` by authoring validation and evaluates
+   `mix(1, texture.r, strength)`.
+4. StandardLit composes scalar factors with texture data as
+   `roughness = roughness_factor * texture.g` and
+   `metallic = metallic_factor * texture.b`. Occlusion modulates only the
+   indirect/ambient StandardLit contribution; direct lighting, ToonLit, and
+   Unlit are not darkened by AO.
+5. Normal, metallic/roughness, and occlusion slots are linear numeric data under
+   ADR 0118. Base color, emissive, toon ramp, and sphere/matcap remain sRGB color
+   slots. The GPU upload cache therefore uses the existing explicit
+   `LinearData` path for all three PBR data textures.
+6. Format parsers normalize source semantics into the generic IR. glTF maps its
+   packed metallic-roughness texture, occlusion texture, normal scale, and
+   occlusion strength directly. Formats without an equivalent input supply the
+   generic defaults (`None`, scale/strength `1.0`) rather than causing runtime
+   format checks.
+7. A missing source tangent may be generated with a MikkTSpace-compatible basis
+   at the generic renderer mesh-preparation boundary. Source tangents remain
+   authoritative. Generation failure or degenerate UV geometry retains ADR
+   0119's zero-handedness sentinel and derivative fallback instead of inventing
+   an arbitrary frame.
+8. The MikkTSpace implementation is a renderer GPU dependency and is isolated
+   behind `engine-render-runtime`'s `gpu` feature. Contract-only consumers such
+   as the importer continue to depend on render-runtime with default features
+   disabled, preserving ADR 0114's lightweight dependency graph.
+
+## Compatibility and Migration
+
+- Material schema v2 files are intentionally rejected after this change. The
+  repository's current writers, fixtures, and imported-material extraction all
+  emit schema v3 in the same change.
+- Existing Material/Texture stable IDs and imported sub-asset ID derivation are
+  unchanged.
+- `Vertex::LAYOUT`, the separate tangent stream from ADR 0119, and public
+  rendering APIs are unchanged.
+- The renderer receives only normalized material and mesh data; there is no
+  glTF-, FBX-, or MMD-specific shader or render path.
+
+## Consequences
+
+- StandardLit can consume the core metallic-roughness and occlusion inputs used
+  by modern content pipelines without waiting for IBL.
+- The same material contract becomes the future input to irradiance/prefiltered
+  environment lighting rather than requiring another importer-specific bridge.
+- Authored source tangents stay byte-for-byte authoritative while assets that do
+  not provide them can gain a stable basis without changing the public vertex
+  contract.
+
+## Verification
+
+- Material v3 round-trip tests cover the new texture IDs and scalar controls,
+  and v2 is explicitly rejected.
+- glTF import tests cover packed metallic/roughness, occlusion, normal scale,
+  and occlusion strength without the previous unsupported-texture diagnostic.
+- Runtime tests verify authoring-to-runtime scalar mapping and linear-data slot
+  classification.
+- Tangent-generation tests verify a UV-mapped quad produces a valid tangent and
+  that explicit source tangents remain authoritative.
+- Because the tangent generator changes the workspace lockfile, Windows
+  Validation runs in `full` mode after the dependency lands.
